[{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":17,"col":17},"end":{"line":18,"col":96}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.update` changes `built[*][*]` in place, and the checker cannot show that\nnothing else still holds the list.\n\n17|                Dict.update built 1 λold →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n6|shared = [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: Main.shared is a top-level\nvalue; the callee writes it only through an approximate step."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":18,"col":27},"end":{"line":18,"col":95}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`List.map` changes a list it is handed in place, and the checker cannot show\nthat nothing else still holds the list.\n\n18|                    Just (List.map (Maybe.withDefault old []) λchild → List.append child [ 9 ])\n                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: Dict.update hands its\nparameter 1 an element of built, whose elements may share one list."}]
